FreeIPMI 1.7.1 - XX/XX/XX
-------------------------

Backwards Compatibility / Legacy Support removal
------------------------------------------------

o Remove support for legacy config file paths
  - /etc/freeipmi.conf (use /etc/freeipmi/freeipmi.conf)
  - /etc/ipmidetect.conf (use /etc/freeipmi/ipmidetect.conf)
  - /etc/ipmidetectd.conf (use /etc/freeipmi/ipmidetectd.conf)
  - /etc/ipmi_monitoring_sensors.conf (use
      /etc/freeipmi/freeipmi_interpret_sensor.conf)
o Remove many legacy long options in tools
  - --no-probing (use --disable-auto-probe)
  - --reg-space (use --register-spacing)
  - --timeout (use --session-timeout)
  - --retry-timeout (use --retransmission-timeout)
  - --auth-type (use --authentication-type)
  - --privilege (use --privilege-level)
  - --priv-level (use --privilege-level)
  - --config (use --config-file)
  - -f (use --flush-cache)
  - -q (use --quiet-cache)
o Remove legacy options in tools
  - Do not support "plain" as an authentication type.
o Remove legacy config file options
  - timeout (use session-timeout)
  - retry-timeout (use retransmission-timeout)
  - cipher_suite_id (use cipher-suite-id)
  - privilege (use privilege-level)
o Remove legacy output support in ipmi-sensors and ipmi-sel.
  - ipmimonitoring legacy output support is also removed as a result.
o libfreeipmi/sel: Remove legacy output support.  Flag
  IPMI_SEL_STRING_FLAGS_LEGACY is now illegal.
o Remove legacy command line options in ipmipower
  - --ipmi-version (--driver-type since 0.7.1)
  - --retry-wait-timeout (--retransmission-wait-timeout since 0.5.1)
  - --retry-backoff-count (--retransmission-backoff-count since 0.5.1)
o Remove legacy config file support for ipmipower (use freeipmi.conf)
o Remove legacy config file options in ipmipower
  - ipmi-version (use driver-type)
  - on-if-off (use ipmipower-on-if-off)
  - wait-until-on (use ipmipower-wait-until-on)
  - wait-until-off (use ipmipower-wait-until-off)
  - retry-wait-timeout (use ipmipower-retransmission-wait-timeout)
  - retransmission-wait-timeout (use ipmipower-retransmission-wait-timeout)
  - retry-backoff-count (use ipmipower-retransmission-backoff-count)
  - retransmission-backoff-count (use ipmipower-retransmission-backoff-count)
  - ping-interval (use ipmipower-ping-interval)
  - ping-timeout (use ipmipower-ping-timeout)
  - ping-packet-count (use ipmipower-ping-packet-count)
  - ping-percent (use ipmipower-ping-percent)
  - ping-consec-count (use ipmipower-ping-consec-count)
o Remove legacy ipmipower prompt options
  - ipmi_version (use driver-type)
  - ipmi-version (use driver-type)
  - hostnames (use hostname)
  - timeout (use session-timeout)
  - retry-timeout (use retransmission-timeout)
  - authentication_type (use authentication-type)
  - cipher_suite_id (use cipher-suite-id)
  - privilege (use privilege-level)
  - retry-wait-timeout (use retransmission-wait-timeout)
  - retry-backoff-count (use retransmission-backoff-count)
  - advanced (use help)
  - network (use help)
o Remove legacy config file support for ipmiconsole (use freeipmi.conf)
o Remove legacy config file options in ipmiconsole
  - escape-char (use ipmiconsole-escape-char)
  - dont-steal (use ipmiconsole-dont-steal)
  - lock-memory (use ipmiconsole-lock-memory)
o Remove legacy command line options in ipmi-sensors
  - --sensors (use --record-ids)
  - --group (use --sensor-types)
  - --groups (use --sensor-types)
  - --sensor-type (use --sensor-types)
  - --exclude-groups (use --exclude-sensor-types)
  - --list-groups (use --list-sensor-types)
  - --sensor-config-file (from ipmimonitoring, use --sensor-state-config-file)
o Remove legacy config file options for ipmi-sensors
  - ipmi-sensors-sensor-config-file (use ipmi-sensors-sensor-state-config-file)
  - ipmi-sensors-groups (use ipmi-sensors-sensor-types)
  - ipmi-sensors-exclude-groups (use ipmi-sensors-exclude-sensor-types)
  - ipmimonitoring-X backwards compatibility options (use ipmi-sensors-X instead)
o Remove legacy command line options in ipmi-chassis
  - --get-capabilities (use --get-chassis-capabilities)
  - --get-status (use --get-chassis-status)
o Remove legacy support in ipmi-chassis that has been replaced with
  ipmi-config.  Removed legacy support options include:
  - --set-power-restore-policy
  - --set-power-cycle-interval
  - --set-boot-flags
  - --boot-type
  - --lock-out-reset-button
  - --blank-screen
  - --boot-device
  - --lock-keyboard
  - --clear-cmos
  - --console-redirection
  - --user-password-bypass
  - --force-progress-event-traps
  - --firmware-bios-verbosity
  - --get-boot-flags
o Remove legacy command line options in ipmi-sel
  - --delete-all (use --clear)
  - --assume-system-event-records (use -W assumesystemevent)
o Remove legacy command line option --skip-checks in ipmi-fru (use -W
  skipchecks)
o Remove legacy command line option --guid in bmc-info (use
  --get-device-id)
o Remove legacy command line options in ipmi-raw
  - --channel-number (use --target-channel-number)
  - --slave-address (use --target-slave-address)
o Remove legacy command line option -f in ipmi-config (use --filename)
o Remove legacy config options in ipmi-config
  - Serial_Conf:Call_Retry_time (is now Call_Retry_Interval)
  - User:Password20 (is now just Password)
  - User:Lan_Enable_Restrict_to_Callback (is now Lan_Enable_Restricted_to_Callback)
  - User:Serial_Enable_Restrict_to_Callback (is now Serial_Enable_Restricted_to_Callback)
o Remove legacy --logfile option to bmc-watchdog.
o Remove legacy OEM Dell commands
  - get-power-info (use get-power-consumption-data)
  - reset-power-info (use reset-power-consumption-data)
  - get-power-supplyinfo (use power-supply-info)
  - get-instantaneous-power-consumption-info (use get-instantaneous-power-consumption-data)
  - get-power-headroom-info (use get-power-head-room)
  - get-average-power-history (use get-power-consumption-data)
  - get-peak-power-history (use get-power-consumption-data)
o Remove legacy OEM Dell commands moved to Inventec
  - get-board-id
  - set-board-id
  - get-fcb-version
  - set-fcb-version
  - get-sol-inactivity-timeout
  - set-sol-inactivity-timeout
o Remove legacy OEM Dell command options / keys
  - "product-name" key for get-system-info command (use "platform-model-name")
  - "slot-number" key for get-system-info command (use "blade-slot-info")
o Remove legacy OEM Inventec commands
  - get-nic-status (use get-nic-mode)
  - set-nic-status (use set-nic-mode)
o Remove legacy OEM IntelNM commands
  - get-node-manager-alert-thresholds (use get-node-manager-policy-alert-thresholds)
  - set-node-manager-alert-thresholds (use set-node-manager-policy-alert-thresholds)
o Remove legacy input options in OEM IntelNM commands:
  - get-node-manager-capabilities policytrigger - remove "inlet" support (use "inlettemperaturelimitpolicytrigger")
  - set-node-manager-policy policytrigger - remove "inlet" support (use "inlettemperaturelimitpolicytrigger")
o Remove legacy command line option --config_file in ipmidetectd (use
  --config-file)
o Remove legacy short option -o in ipmidetect (use -h)

